{"repositoryId":488365405,"availability":"available","full":"gavr123456789/Niva","name":"Niva","description":"Smalltalk like programming language","category":"Developer tools","language":"Kotlin","stars":76,"forks":3,"created":"2022-05-03T21:16:15Z","updated":"2026-10-18T02:57:19Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gavr123456789.github.io/niva-site","topics":["compiler","kotlin","language","programming-language","smalltalk","tagged-unions","typed"],"demo":"https://gavr123456789.github.io/niva-site","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.403Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.403Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.403Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.403Z","stars":76,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Docs | Learn X in Y minutes | Installation | Libs","Niva is a simple language that takes a lot of inspiration from Smalltalk. But leaning towards the functional side and static types. Everything is still an object, but instead of classes, interfaces, inheritance, and abstract classes, we have tagged unions, which is the only way to achieve polymorphism.","In essence, niva is highly minimalistic, since its ancestor is Smalltalk. It introduces types, unions, and associated methods. Yes there are no functions."],"features":["Simple expression-based syntax inspired by Smalltalk","Smalltalk-like hierarchy: projects -> packages -> protocols -> methods","Everything is an object, and every method has a receiver (this/self)","So methods can be defined for core types like Int or List (unlike in Go)","Methods are not tied to a type declaration; you can define a new method in a different file (like in Go)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gavr123456789/Niva/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"58971fc7cf62c961d277b281b038c49d40971e5709c5b437598e8823e8211b03","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.488Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:06.488Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatIt